    Text = "The event has ended. Currently, only the \"Rite of Benediction\" is available."
  },
  Activity_116470_ActivityTips = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Event Overview>
1. During the event, Keepers can collect event currency "Audience Oblation," "Contrite Oblation," and "Devoted Oblation" through the limited-time gameplay "Shared Bitter Blood" and "Achievement Rewards". "Audience Oblation," "Contrite Oblation," and "Devoted Oblation" can be used to purchase items in the "Rite of Benediction," including the event-exclusive SR Wheel of Destiny "The Divus' Visage," Luminous Core, Pure Core, and more. 
2. During the event, "Dreamscape: Beyond the Skies: Part II" will be available for limited free access. Completing event achievements will also grant the event-exclusive avatar "By the Silver Key: Pollux"!

<Title:Event Duration>
1. October 20, 9:00 - November 3, 9:00 (GMT+8), all event gameplay can be participated in. 
2. November 3, 9:00 - November 10, 9:00 (GMT+8), only "Rite of Benediction" and Achievement Rewards can be participated in. 

<Title:Shared Bitter Blood>
1. "Shared Bitter Blood" consists of 7 stages, with 1 stage automatically opening each day. 
2. Each challenge will consume 120 Menophin, and a successful challenge will yield event currency. 
3. After clearing a stage, the "Reenact" function for that stage will be unlocked. Please note: using the "Reenact" function will not yield Affinity. 
4. You can use Alumnis to assist you in clearing stages more easily. 

<Title: Vortex of Memory>
 After the event starts, you will automatically receive 60 "Audience Oblation" every hour, with a maximum storage of 25 hours. 

<Title:Rite of Benediction>
1. The "Rite of Benediction" has three shops, with the following opening times:
"Ablution of Flesh": Opens at 9:00 on October 20.
"Contrition of Soul": Opens at 9:00 on October 21.
"Exaction of Sins": Opens at 9:00 on October 22. 
2. Each exchange will consume 750 "Audience Oblation"/"Contrite Oblation"/"Devoted Oblation," randomly obtaining five item rewards from the studio. 
3. The item rewards from each studio are divided into "Special Items" and "Common Items". Resets can restore the remaining quantity of "Special Items" to the maximum limit, with the specific rules as follows: 
(1) For the first 2 resets: When there are no remaining "Special Items," the Keeper can choose to reset, which will restore the remaining quantities of "Special Items" and "Common Items" to the maximum limit; or continue to exchange. When there are no remaining "Common Items," a reset must be performed to continue exchanging. 
(2) From the 3rd reset onward: A reset can only be performed when there are no remaining "Common Items". The reset will restore the remaining quantity of "Common Items" to the maximum limit, and "Special Items" will no longer reset. 

<Title:Event Bonuses>
1. Keepers who possess specific Awakeners or Wheels of Destiny (not required to be in the lineup) can earn extra drop bonuses for "Audience Oblation," "Contrite Oblation," and "Devoted Oblation" from the tasks in "Shared Bitter Blood". The specific bonuses are as follows:
Awakener "Pollux": Enlighten 0/1/2/3 and above, bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%.
SSR Wheel of Destiny "Twisted Knight Ballad": Ascension 0/1/2/3 and above, bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%.
SR Wheel of Destiny "The Divus' Visage": Ascension 0/1/2/3 and above, bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%. 
2. Different Awakeners or Wheels of Destiny's "event bonuses" will be calculated cumulatively. 
3. Notably, the rewards for the first completion challenge of Madness Difficulty will not be affected by "event bonuses". 

<Title:Dreamscape>
1. During the event, "Dreamscape: Beyond the Skies: Part II" can be unlocked for free. 
2. After the event ends, the investigation progress of "Dreamscape: Beyond the Skies: Part II" will be retained. Completing any unfinished investigation events during the event will also yield investigation rewards consistent with the event period. If "Dreamscape: Beyond the Skies: Part II" was not unlocked during the event, it can still be unlocked after the event by consuming "Reality Verge" *7. 
3. Regardless of whether it was during the event, clearing "Dreamscape: Beyond the Skies: Part II" will grant "Posse: Sacred Bleeding Heart".]]
  },
