  Activity_124051_ActivityName = {
    Text = "Abyss Sacrifice: Rerun"
  },
  Activity_124051_ActivityPlot = {
    Text = [[
On the reflection of the deep ocean, her King's dream dissipates, and the Divine Realm decays.
She emerges from ancient dreams, stepping into the ruins of a collapsing future.
She questions the Abyss, but the Abyss remains silent.
She offers sacrifices to the Abyss, only to hear her own echo.]]
  },
  Activity_124051_ActivityStageEndContent = {
    Text = "Event has Ended. Currently only \"The Abyss Responds\" is available."
  },
  Activity_124051_ActivityTips = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Event Overview>
1. During the event period, Keepers can collect event currency through limited-time gameplay "Divine Rebirth," "Sovereign's Decree," and "Achievement Rewards." The event currency can be used in "The Abyss Responds" for offerings to obtain item rewards, including the limited-time SR Wheel of Destiny "Deep Sea's Call," Aetheric Stone, Pure Core, Ethereal Core, and more.
2. During the event, "Dreamscape: Desecrate" will be available for free. Completing event achievements will also grant the limited-time avatar "By the Silver Key: Miryam"!

<Title:Event Time>
1. March 9, 9:00 - March 23, 9:00 (GMT+8), all event content is available for participation.
2. March 23, 9:00 - March 30, 9:00 (GMT+8), only "The Abyss Responds" and "Achievement Rewards" will remain, other content will have ended and cannot be participated in.

<Title: Divine Rebirth>
1. "Divine Rebirth" consists of 5 stages, with 1 stage automatically opening every 2 days.
2. Each challenge will consume 120 Menophin, and successful challenges will reward event currency.
3. After clearing a stage, the "Reenact" feature for that stage will be unlocked. Please note: using the "Reenact" feature will not grant Affinity.
4. You can use Alumni Association support and "Ritual: Abyssal Offering" to help you clear stages more easily.

<Title: Sacrificial Boon>
1. Keepers with specific Awakeners or Wheels of Destiny (not required to be in the lineup) can gain extra drop bonuses for "Sacrificial Tears," "Sacrificial Blood," and "Sacrificial Marrow" in the rewards for "Divine Rebirth" stage tasks (including Reenact), with the following bonuses:
Awakener "Miryam": Enlighten 0/1/2/3 and above, bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%
SSR Wheel of Destiny "Power of the Pious": Ascension 0/1/2/3 and above, bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%
SR Wheel of Destiny "Deep Sea's Call": Ascension 0/1/2/3 and above, bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%
2. Different Awakeners or Wheels of Destiny's "Sacrificial Boon" will be calculated cumulatively. 
3. Notably, the first completion challenge reward for Madness Difficulty will not be affected by "Sacrificial Boon."

<Title: Resonance: Abyssal Offering>
1. Keepers can obtain "Heart of Devoutness" by completing event achievements. 
2. Consuming "Heart of Devoutness" activates "Resonance: Abyssal Offering," allowing for the following bonuses:
(1) Makes Keepers stronger in the event gameplay "Divine Rebirth," making challenges easier.
(2) Increases the event currency obtained after completing "Divine Rebirth" challenges.
(3) Activates the event gameplay "Sovereign's Decree."

<Title: Sovereign's Decree>
After activating the resonance "Trial by Sacrifice," you will automatically receive 60 "Sacrificial Tears" per hour, with a maximum storage of 25 hours.

<Title: The Abyss Responds>
1. "The Abyss Responds" has three altars, with the following opening times:
"Alter of Tears": March 9, 9:00 ~ March 30, 9:00.
"Alter of Blood": March 11, 9:00 ~ March 30, 9:00.
"Alter of Souls": March 13, 9:00 ~ March 30, 9:00.
2. Each offering will consume 750 "Sacrificial Tears"/"Sacrificial Blood"/"Sacrificial Marrow," randomly awarding five item rewards from the altar.
3. The item rewards from each altar are categorized as "Special Items" and "Common Items." When resetting, you can reset the remaining quantity of designated item rewards to the maximum limit, with specific rules as follows:
(1) For the first 3 resets: When "Special Items" have no remaining quantity, Keepers can choose to reset, which will reset the remaining quantities of "Special Items" and "Common Items" to the maximum limit; they can also choose to continue offering items. When "Common Items" also have no remaining quantity, a reset is required to continue offering items.
(2) Starting from the 4th reset: A reset can only be performed when "Common Items" have no remaining quantity, which will reset the remaining quantity of "Common Items" to the maximum limit, and "Special Items" will no longer be reset.

<Title: Dreamscape>
1. During the event, "Dreamscape: Desecrate" will be available for free.
2. After the event ends, the investigation progress for "Dreamscape: Desecrate" will be retained. If "Dreamscape: Desecrate" was not unlocked during the event, it can still be unlocked after the event by consuming "Reality Verge" *7.
3. Regardless of whether during the event, clearing "Dreamscape: Desecrate" will grant "Posse: Festival of Tides."

<Title: Rerun Compensation>
1. Keepers who previously unlocked "Dreamscape: Desecrate" will receive a compensation of "Sacrificial Tears" *700 when re-unlocking during this rerun event.
2. Keepers who previously obtained the limited-time avatar "By the Silver Key: Miryam," when obtained again, will automatically convert to "Formless One's Invitation" *1.
3. Keepers who previously obtained the resonance activation material "Heart of Devoutness," each additional "Heart of Devoutness" will automatically convert to "Rose Scrip" *5000.
]]
  },
