  Activity_125364_ActivityStageEndContent = {
    Text = "Event has ended. Currently, only \"Desolate Offering\" is available."
  },
  Activity_125364_ActivityTips = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Event Overview>
During the event, Keepers can collect the event currency "Pear Syrup Candy" through the limited-time gameplay "Obsidian Matriarch" and "Achievement Rewards". "Pear Syrup Candy" can be exchanged for rewards in "Desolate Offering," including the event-exclusive SR Wheel of Destiny "Magnolia's Lure," Luminous Core, Pure Core, Aetheric Shard, Mimetic Crystal, and more.

<Title:Obsidian Matriarch>
1. "Obsidian Matriarch" consists of 9 material stages that can be directly battled without exploration, with one stage opening each day.
2. Each challenge will consume 120 Menophin, and successful challenges will yield cultivation materials and event currency.
3. After clearing a stage, the "Reenact" feature for that stage will be unlocked. Please note: Using the "Reenact" feature will not grant Affinity.
4. You can use Alumni Assistance to help you clear stages more easily.

<Title:Event Bonuses>
1. Keepers who possess specific Awakeners or Wheels of Destiny (not required to be deployed) can gain additional drop bonuses for "Pear Syrup Candy" in the "Obsidian Matriarch" stage tasks (including Reenact). The specific bonuses are as follows: 
 Awakener "Xu": Enlighten 0/1/2/3 and above, bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%
 SSR Wheel of Destiny "Vain Regrets": Ascension 0/1/2/3 and above, bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%
 SR Wheel of Destiny "Magnolia's Lure": Ascension 0/1/2/3 and above, bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%
2. Different Awakeners or Wheels of Destiny's "Event Bonuses" will be calculated in an additive manner.
3. Notably, the first completion challenge rewards for Madness Difficulty will not be affected by the aforementioned bonuses. 

<Title:Desolate Offering>
1. Each "Offering" will consume 750 "Pear Syrup Candy" and randomly grant five item rewards from "Desolate Offering". 
2. The item rewards from "Desolate Offering" are divided into "Special Items" and "Common Items". When resetting, the remaining quantity of special item rewards can be reset to the limit, with specific rules as follows: 
(1) For the first 5 resets: When there are no remaining "Special Items," Keepers can choose to reset, which will reset the remaining quantities of "Special Items" and "Common Items" to the limit; Keepers can also choose to continue exchanging, and when there are no remaining "Common Items," a reset must be performed to continue exchanging. 
(2) Starting from the 6th reset: A reset can only be performed when there are no remaining "Common Items," and the reset will reset the remaining quantity of "Common Items" to the limit, while "Special Items" will no longer be reset. 

<Title:Psyche Deepdive>
1. During the event, "Whispers Behind the Fan" can be unlocked for free.
2. After the event ends, the investigation progress for "Whispers Behind the Fan" will be retained. Completing any investigation events that were not finished during the event will still grant the same investigation rewards as during the event. If "Whispers Behind the Fan" was not unlocked during the event, it can still be unlocked after the event ends by consuming "Reality Verge"*3.
3. Regardless of whether it was during the event or not, clearing "Psyche Deepdive: Whispers Behind the Fan" will grant you the "Posse: Manor Echoes."

<Title:Event Time>
1. January 26th, 9:00 - February 9th, 9:00 (GMT+8), all content in the event overview is available for participation. 
2. February 9th, 9:00 - February 16th, 9:00 (GMT+8), only "Desolate Offering" and "Achievement Rewards" will remain, and all other content will have ended and be unavailable for participation. 
3. After February 16th, 9:00 (GMT+8), any unexchanged "Pear Syrup Candy" will be reclaimed at a rate of 40 "Rose Scrip". Please check your inbox to claim them in time.]]
  },
