  Activity_52040_ActivityStageEndContent = {
    Text = "Event has Ended. Currently only \"The Abyss Responds\" is available."
  },
  Activity_52040_ActivityTips = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Event Overview>
1. During the event, Keepers can collect event currency through limited-time plays "the Divine Realm Emergence," "King's Decree," and "Achievement Rewards." The event currency can be used in "Abyssal Response" to obtain item rewards, including the event-exclusive SR Wheel of Destiny "Call of the Deep," Philosopher's Stone, Pure Core, and Luminous Core.
2. "Dreamscape: Desecration" will be freely accessible during the event.

<Title:Event Duration>
1. From 9:00 June 17 to 9:00 July 1 (GMT+8), all event content will be available.
2. From 9:00 July 1 to 9:00 July 8 (GMT+8), only "Abyssal Response" and "Achievement Rewards" will be available; other content will be inaccessible.

<Title:the Divine Realm Emergence>
1. "the Divine Realm Emergence" includes 5 stages, unlocking one every 2 days.
2. Each challenge costs 120 Menophin, and successful challenges grant event currency "Sacrificial Tears," "Sacrificial Blood," and "Sacrificial Marrow." For double rewards, 240 Menophin is required, and while mission rewards double, affinity rewards remain unchanged.
3. After achieving 100% "Achievement Rewards," you unlock the "Re-enact" function for cleared stages. Each "Re-enact" uses 120 Menophin. Note: No affinity is gained through "Re-enact."
4. You can use Alumni aid and "Resonance: Abyssal Ceremony" to assist in clearing the stages.

<Title:Offering Bonus>
1. Certain Awakeners or Wheels of Destiny (don't need to be deployed) owned by Keepers increase the drop rate of "Sacrificial Tears," "Sacrificial Blood," and "Sacrificial Marrow" in "the Divine Realm Emergence" (including re-enactment). Bonuses are:
Awakener "Miryam": Enlighten 0/1/2/3+; Bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%
SSR Wheel of Destiny "Devout Power": Enhance 0/1/2/3+; Bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%
SR Wheel of Destiny "Call of the Deep": Enhance 0/1/2/3+; Bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%
2. Bonuses from different Awakeners or Wheels of Destiny stack.

<Title:Resonance: Abyssal Ceremony>
1. Keepers can obtain "Devout Heart" by completing event achievements.
2. Using "Devout Heart" to activate "Resonance: Abyssal Ceremony" grants the following bonuses:
(1) Strengthen Keepers in "the Divine Realm Emergence" for easier challenges.
(2) Increase event currency from "the Divine Realm Emergence" challenges.
(3) Unlock the event play "King's Decree."

<Title:King's Decree>
Activating the "Sacrificial Trial" resonance grants 60 "Sacrificial Tears" every hour, storing up to 25 hours.

<Title:Abyssal Response>
1. "Abyssal Response" features three altars, unlocking as follows:
"Altar of Tears": Opens at 9:00 June 17.
"Altar of Blood": Opens at 9:00 June 19.
"Altar of Souls": Opens at 9:00 June 21.
2. Each offering consumes 500 "Sacrificial Tears"/"Sacrificial Blood"/"Sacrificial Marrow" and grants five random item rewards from the altar.
3. Each altar's item rewards are categorized as "Blessings of the Divine Realm" and "Mundane Rewards." Resetting can replenish specified item quantities:
(1) First two resets: When "Blessings of the Divine Realm" are depleted, Keepers can choose to reset, replenishing "Blessings of the Divine Realm" and "Mundane Rewards" quantities; continuing offerings is allowed until "Mundane Rewards" deplete, requiring a reset to continue offerings.
(2) From the third reset: Only "Mundane Rewards" are replenished upon reset, "Blessings of the Divine Realm" are not.

<Title:Dreamscape>
1. "Dreamscape" is a new investigation type, emphasizing textual representation over typical story playthroughs.
2. In "Dreamscape: Desecration," you will link with Miryam's spirit to read her memories, witnessing her childhood struggles in Lemuria, her faith-driven confusion and struggles, and her path to becoming a savior and destroyer...
3. "Dreamscape: Desecration" will be free during the event. New events will launch every 2 days, and clearing it grants Silver and the event-exclusive SR Wheel of Destiny "Call of the Deep" in achievement rewards, only available during the event.
4. After the event, "Dreamscape: Desecration" progress will be retained. If not unlocked during the event, it can be unlocked post-event using 7 "Reality Verges."
5. Regardless of the event period, clearing "Dreamscape: Desecration" grants a "Posse: Sea Sacrifice."



]]
  },
