  Activity_66375_ActivityName = {
    Text = "Final Battle: Primordial Shades"
  },
  Activity_66375_ActivityPlot = {
    Text = [[
Its Gaze swept across myriad Dimensions, and gazing back were myriad silver figures. 
They are small, Fragile. They fight to remember, until death claims them.]]
  },
  Activity_66375_ActivityStageEndContent = {
    Text = "Event objectives achieved. You may proceed to continue the investigation."
  },
  Activity_66375_ActivityTips = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Cooperative Battle: Primordial>
The "Cooperative Battle: Primordial" consists of 7 unrepeatable levels that directly challenge the Vision of the Primordial. The first 3 levels will open on the first day of the event, and then 1 level will open every 3 days.
Each time you successfully challenge the corresponding Vision of the Primordial, you will receive the corresponding reward.
Each type of Vision of the Primordial has multiple clones. Whenever any Keeper successfully challenges a certain type of Vision of the Primordial, the "World Residue Count" of that type will decrease by 1. When all clones of that type are defeated, the corresponding level will close and cannot be challenged again.
All levels are affected by the "D-tide of Regional D-effect: End," but each level will provide different "Pure Core" Relics, which will grant you powerful bonuses. In addition, each level will also provide an "Eye of Gnosis" Relic, which will grant Tawil 120 Aliemus at the start of the battle, increasing all Damage, Shields, and Healing effects caused by Tawil by 50%.
All levels must choose assistance. During the entire event, each mutually following Keeper can only provide you with assistance once. Due to the use of assistance, the actual Affinity reward will increase by another 50% on top of the base reward.
Keepers must complete Investigation Operations 2-9 at least to participate in this event.

<Title:Investigation Operation: Final Chapter>
The main body of each Vision of the Primordial still needs to be defeated by you in Investigation Operations 9-5 to 9-11. These special levels have no achievements, no star ratings, cannot use the "Eye of Gnosis" Relic or assistance, and are more difficult.
After the "Cooperative Battle: Primordial" event ends, the subsequent levels of "Investigation Operation: Final Chapter" will be unlocked. When you collectively defeat all clones of various Visions of the Primordial with other Keepers, you can unlock the corresponding levels in Investigation Operations 9-5 to 9-11 in advance.]]
  },
  Activity_66375_BannerText = {
    Text = "Limited-Time Event Now Available!"
  },
  Activity_66908_ActivityName = {
    Text = "Breath of Fertility"
  },
  Activity_66908_ActivityTips = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Event Rules>
During the "Bountiful Breath" event, Keepers can use system preset teams containing Thais to experience designated levels an unlimited number of times.
When playing through event levels, adjustments to the Awakener in the team lineup cannot be made.
<Title:Activity Rewards>
After successfully completing a level challenge for the first time, you can claim trial rewards from the event interface.]]
  },
  Activity_67077_ActivityName = {
    Text = "Echoed Pilgrimage IX"
  },
  Activity_67077_ActivityPlot = {
    Text = "Fleeting Memory sealed and archived, a journey recorded into the past. In moments of remembrance, do not forget to offer your reverent Tribute."
  },
  Activity_67718_ActivityName = {
    Text = "Before Spring Fades: Rerun"
  },
  Activity_67718_ActivityPlot = {
    Text = [[
The laughter of the girls echoes in the garden before the fire starts.
Pause for this beautiful past, my friend.
Listen to the stories of the unfaded spring, softly narrated.]]
  },
  Activity_67718_ActivityStageEndContent = {
    Text = "The event has ended. Currently, only \"Colette's Floral House\" is available."
  },
  Activity_67718_ActivityTips = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Event Overview>
1. During the event, Keepers can collect three types of "Poems" via the limited-time gameplay "Garden Memories," "Muse's Kiss," and "Achievement Rewards". Poems can be exchanged for item rewards in "Colette's Flowerhouse," including the event-limited SR Destiny Wheel "Poetic Bygone Days," Pure Core, Ethereal Core, Aetheric Shard, Mimetic Crystal, etc.
2. "Task Record: Rose Habitat" will be freely accessible during the event.

<Title:Event Duration>
1. August 10, 9:00 - September 7, 9:00 (GMT+8): All event content is available.
2. September 7, 9:00 - September 14, 9:00 (GMT+8): Only "Colette's Flowerhouse" and "Achievement Rewards" remain accessible; other content ends.

<Title:Garden Memories>
1. "Garden Memories" includes 5 levels, each unlocking every 2 days.
2. Each challenge consumes 120 Menophin. Successful challenges yield event currency "Poems of Sorrow," "Poems of Regret," and "Poems of Joy".
3. Upon clearing a level, the "Replay" feature is unlocked. Note: "Replay" does not provide Affinity.
4. Alumni assistance and "Resonance: Garden Elegy" can help you clear levels more easily.
5. Note: Madness difficulty does not consume Menophin, cannot be replayed, and no event currency is rewarded for subsequent challenges after the first clear.

<Title:Poem Bonus>
1. Keepers possessing certain Awakeners or Destiny Wheels (no deployment required) can get bonus drops of "Poems of Sorrow," "Poems of Regret," and "Poems of Joy" from "Garden Memories" level rewards (including in Replay mode). Bonuses are as follows:
Awakener "Horla": Enlighten 0/1/2/3+, Bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%
SSR Destiny Wheel "The Last Verse": Stacks 0/1/2/3+, Bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%
SR Destiny Wheel "Poetic Bygone Days": Stacks 0/1/2/3+, Bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%
2. Bonuses from different Awakeners or Destiny Wheels stack.
3. Particularly, the first clear rewards of Madness difficulty are not affected by Poem Bonus.

<Title:Resonance: Garden Elegy>
1. Keepers can obtain "Heart of Ashes" by completing event achievements.
2. Consume "Heart of Ashes" to activate "Resonance: Garden Elegy" to gain the following bonuses:
(1) Make Keepers stronger in "Garden Memories," making challenges easier.
(2) Increase event currency rewards from "Garden Memories" challenges.
(3) Unlock the event gameplay "Muse's Kiss".

<Title:Muse's Kiss>
After activating Resonance "Everything Grows," you automatically get 60 "Poems of Sorrow" every hour, up to 25 hours.
After activating Resonance "Exchange Poem for Flower," "Muse's Kiss" will also generate 60 "Poems of Regret" every hour.

<Title:Colette's Flowerhouse>
1. "Colette's Flowerhouse" has three gardens, opening as follows:
"Iris garden": Opens at 9:00 on August 10.
"Platycodon Flower Bed": Opens at 9:00 on August 12.
"Rose garden": Opens at 9:00 on August 14.
2. Each exchange consumes 750 "Poems of Sorrow"/"Poems of Regret"/"Poems of Joy," granting five random item rewards from the garden.
3. Each garden's item rewards are categorized as "Special Items" and "Common Items". Resetting restores the remaining quantity of special items, rules are as follows:
(1) First 2 resets: When no "Special Items" remain, Keepers can choose to reset, which restores the remaining quantities of both "Special" and "Common Items"; Keepers can also continue exchanging. When no "Common Items" remain, resetting is required to continue exchanging.
(2) From the 3rd reset onward: Resetting is only possible when no "Common Items" remain, which restores "Common Items" only; "Special Items" do not reset.
4. On September 14, 9:00 (GMT+8), unexchanged "Poems" are converted to 40 "Rose Scrip" per Poem, collected via in-game mail.

<Title:Task Record>
1. "Task Record: Rose Habitat" will be freely accessible during the event. A new event launches every 2 days. Clearing "Task Record: Rose Habitat" grants Silver Prime, the event-limited SR Destiny Wheel "Poetic Bygone Days," etc., in Achievement Rewards. Achievement rewards are only accessible during the event and cannot be completed or claimed after the event ends.
2. After the event, investigation progress of "Task Record: Rose Habitat" is retained. If "Task Record: Rose Habitat" is not unlocked during the event, it can still be unlocked after the event by consuming 7 "Reality Verge".
3. Regardless of event duration, clearing "Task Record: Rose Habitat" grants "Posse: Spring's Verse".]]
  },
