  Activity_67745_ActivityTips = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Event Overview>
1. During the event, Keepers can collect three types of "Buds" through limited-time gameplay "Beast Ambition" and "Achievements." These "Buds" can be exchanged for item rewards in "Mountain Maw," including the event-exclusive SR Wheel of Destiny "Til the Snow Melts," Pure Core, Luminous Core, Aetheric Shard, Mimetic Crystal, and more.
2. The "Special Ops: Elworth's Returnee" will be available for free during the event.

<Title:Event Duration>
1. From 9:00 on July 13 to 9:00 on August 10 (GMT+8), all event content is accessible.
2. From 9:00 on August 10 to 9:00 on August 17 (GMT+8), only "Mountain Maw" and "Achievements" will remain available; other content will end and become inaccessible.

<Title:Beastly Ambition>
1. "Beastly Ambition" consists of 5 stages, with one stage unlocking every 2 days.
2. Each challenge consumes 120 Menophin, and successful challenges reward event currency: "Frozen Bud," "Silver Frost Bud," and "Sunlight Bud."
3. After clearing a stage, the "Reenact" function unlocks. Note: Using "Reenact" does not grant Affinity.
4. Alumni Support and "Resonance: Devour Mountains" can assist in clearing stages more easily.
5. After clearing any difficulty, the Madness difficulty for that level unlocks. Madness difficulty does not consume Menophin, cannot be replayed, and repeating it after the first clear won't grant additional event currency.
<Title:Bud Bonus>
1. Keepers with specific Awakeners or Wheels of Destiny (not required to be deployed) receive extra drops of "Frozen Bud," "Silver Frost Bud," and "Sunlight Bud" in "Beastly Ambition" stage rewards (including reenacts), as follows:
Awakener "Helot: Catena": Enlighten 0/1/2/3+, 20%/30%/40%/50% bonus
SSR Wheel "Drowning in Crimson": Stack 0/1/2/3+, 20%/30%/40%/50% bonus
SR Wheel "Til the Snow Melts": Stack 0/1/2/3+, 20%/30%/40%/50% bonus
2. Different Awakeners or Wheels' "Bud Bonus" stack.
3. Special note: The first clear reward on Madness difficulty is not affected by "Bud Bonus."

<Title:Resonance: Devour Mountains>
1. Keepers can obtain "Heart of Devouring" by completing event achievements.
2. Consuming "Heart of Devouring" activates "Resonance: Devour Mountains," making the Keepers stronger in "Beastly Ambition" and making challenges easier.

<Title:Mountain Maw>
1. "Mountain Maw" has three exchange stores, opening as follows:
"Insatiable Ambition": Opens at 9:00 on July 13.
"Fury of Vengeance": Opens at 9:00 on July 15.
"Hope for Resurrection": Opens at 9:00 on July 17.
2. Each exchange consumes 750 "Frozen Bud"/"Silver Frost Bud"/"Sunlight Bud," randomly granting five items from the store.
3. Each store has "Special Items" and "Common Items." Resetting restores the remaining quantity of special items to the limit, as follows:
(1) First 2 resets: When "Special Items" are out of stock, Keepers can reset, restoring both "Special Items" and "Common Items" to their limits; alternatively, they can continue exchanging until "Common Items" are also out of stock, requiring a reset to proceed.
(2) From the 3rd reset onward: Resetting is possible only when "Common Items" are out of stock, restoring "Common Items" to their limit while "Special Items" remain unchanged.
4. After 9:00 on August 17 (GMT+8), any remaining "Buds" will be reclaimed at the rate of 40 Rose Scrips per Bud. Check your mail for details.

<Title:Special Ops>
1. "Special Ops: Elworth's Returnee" will be free during the event. Clearing "Special Ops: Elworth's Returnee" earns rewards in Achievements, including Silver and the event-exclusive SR Wheel "Til the Snow Melts," obtainable only during the event. No completion or claimable rewards will be available after the event ends.
2. After the event ends, the investigation progress of "Special Ops: Elworth's Returnee" will remain. If not unlocked during the event, it can still be unlocked using 7 Reality Verge.
3. Regardless of the event period, clearing "Special Ops: Elworth's Returnee" rewards "Posse: The Mountains' Resolve."]]
