  Activity_78652_ActivityStageEndContent = {
    Text = "The event has ended. Currently, only \"Ego Dissection\" is available."
  },
  Activity_78652_ActivityTips = {
    Text = "<Title:Event Overview>\n1. During the event period, Keepers can collect event currency \"Memory Puzzle\" through limited-time activities like \"Memory Coding,\" \"Edge Storage,\" and \"Achievement Rewards.\" \"Memory Puzzle\" can be used to purchase items in \"Persona Analysis,\" including the event-limited SR Wheel of Destiny \"Determination of the Silver Cod,\" the Pure Core, and the Luminous Core.\n2. During the event, \"Special Record: Tranquil Fission\" is available for limited free access. Completing activity achievements will also earn you an event-exclusive avatar \"By the Silver Key: '24'\"!\n\n<Title:Event Duration>\n1. April 21, 9:00 - May 5, 9:00 (GMT+8), all event activities are available.\n2. May 5, 9:00 - May 12, 9:00 (GMT+8), only \"Persona Analysis\" and achievement rewards are available.\n\n<Title:Memory Coding>\n1. \"Memory Coding\" consists of 5 stages, with one stage unlocking automatically every 2 days.\n2. Each challenge consumes 120 Menophin, and successful challenges earn event currency.\n3. After completing a stage, the \"Replay\" function for that stage is unlocked. Note: Using the \"Replay\" function does not grant Affinity.\n4. You can use Alumni assistance and \"Resonance: Dissociative Symptom\" to help ease the challenges.\n\n<Title:Rational Bonuses>\n1. Keepers possessing specific Awakeners or Wheels of Destiny (not required to be deployed) can earn additional drop bonuses for \"Memory Puzzle\" in the \"Memory Coding\" stage rewards. Detailed bonuses are as follows:\nAwakener \"24\": Enlighten 0/1/2/3 and above, 20%/30%/40%/50% bonus.\nSSR Wheel of Destiny \"Aberrant Devour\": Stack 0/1/2/3 and above, 20%/30%/40%/50% bonus.\nSR Wheel of Destiny \"Determination of the Silver Cod\": Stack 0/1/2/3 and above, 20%/30%/40%/50% bonus.\n2. Rational Bonuses from different Awakeners or Wheels of Destiny accumulate additively.\n3. Notably, the first-clear challenge rewards in Madness difficulty are not affected by Rational Bonuses.\n\n<Title:Resonance: Dissociative Symptom>\n1. Keepers can obtain \"Heart of Division\" by completing event achievements.\n2. Consuming \"Heart of Division\" to activate \"Resonance: Dissociative Symptom\" grants the following bonuses:\n(1) Empowers the Keeper in event activities \"Memory Coding\" and \"Special Record: Tranquil Fission,\" making challenges easier.\n(2) Increases the rewards obtained after completing \"Memory Coding\" challenges.\n(3) Activates the event activity \"Edge Storage.\"\n\n<Title:Edge Storage>\n1. After activating the resonance \"Diagnosis: Shattered Self,\" automatically gain 60 \"Memory Puzzle α\" per hour, storing up to 25 hours.\n2. After activating the resonance \"Cognitive Resonance,\" automatically gain 30 \"Memory Puzzle β\" per hour, storing up to 25 hours.\n\n<Title:Special Record>\n1. During the event, \"Special Record: Tranquil Fission\" can be unlocked for free.\n2. Post-event, progress in \"Special Record: Tranquil Fission\" investigations will be retained, and completing incomplete event-period investigations can earn rewards consistent with the event period. If \"Special Record: Tranquil Fission\" wasn't unlocked during the event period, it can still be unlocked post-event by consuming \"Reality Verge\" *7.\n3. Regardless of the event period, completing \"Special Record: Tranquil Fission\" awards \"Posse: All of Her\".\n\n<Title:Replica Compensation>\n1. Keepers who previously unlocked \"Special Record: Tranquil Fission\" during this rerun event will receive compensation of \"Memory Puzzle α\" *700.\n2. Keepers who previously obtained the event-exclusive avatar \"By the Silver Key: '24'\" will have it automatically converted to 1 \"Formless One's Invitation\" upon receiving it again.\n3. Keepers who previously obtained activation resonance material \"Heart of Division\" will have every surplus \"Heart of Division\" automatically converted to \"Rose Scrip\" *5000.\n"
  },
