  Activity_95977_ActivityStageEndContent = {
    Text = "The event has ended, currently only \"Ossuary Banquet\" can be participated in."
  },
  Activity_95977_ActivityTips = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Event Overview>
During the event, Keepers can collect event currency through the limited-time gameplay "Soulsfeast" and "Achievement Rewards". The event currency can be used in the "Ossuary Banquet" to exchange for item rewards, including the limited SR Wheel of Destiny "Macabre Delicacies," Aetheric Stone, Pure Core, Luminous Core, and more.

<Title:Event Duration>
1. July 21 9:00 - August 4 9:00 (GMT+8), all event content is available.
2. August 4 9:00 - August 11 9:00 (GMT+8), only the "Ossuary Banquet" and "Achievement Rewards" remain active; all other content will end and become unavailable.

<Title:Soulsfeast>
1. "Soulsfeast" includes 5 stages, each opening automatically every 2 days.
2. Each challenge consumes 120 Menophin. Successfully completing a challenge grants event currency.
3. Upon clearing a stage, its "Reenact" function becomes unlocked. Please note: Using the "Reenact" function does not grant Affinity.
4. You may use Alumni Co-op to assist you in clearing stages more easily.

<Title:Event Bonuses>
1. Possessing specific Awakener or Wheel of Destiny (not required to be deployed) grants additional drop bonuses for "Rotten Phalanges" in "Soulsfeast" stage rewards (including Reenact). Details are as follows:
Awakener "Doresain": Enlighten 0/1/2/3+, bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%
SSR Wheel of Destiny "Kiss of Repose": Ascension 0/1/2/3+, bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%
SR Wheel of Destiny "Macabre Delicacies": Ascension 0/1/2/3+, bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%
2. Bonuses from different Awakeners or Wheels of Destiny stack.
3. Special Note: First-clear rewards on Madness difficulty are unaffected by these event bonuses.

<Title:Ossuary Banquet>
1. Each "Request Dishes" consumes 750 "Rotten Phalanges" and randomly grants one of five possible item rewards from the "Ossuary Banquet".
2. Item rewards in the "Ossuary Banquet" are divided into "Special Items" and "Common Items". Resetting restores remaining quantities of special items up to their maximum limit. Specific rules are as follows:
(1) First 5 Resets: When no "Special Items" remain, Keepers may choose to reset, restoring both "Special Items" and "Common Items" to their maximum quantities; alternatively, they may continue exchanging. Once "Common Items" also run out, a reset is required before further exchanges can occur.
(2) From the 6th Reset onward: Resetting is allowed only when no "Common Items" remain. After resetting, "Common Items" are restored to their maximum quantity, but "Special Items" are no longer replenished.
3. After August 11 9:00 (GMT+8), any unexchanged "Rotten Phalanges" will be converted into "Rose Scrip*40" at a fixed rate. Please check your mailbox for this conversion.]]
