  Activity_97672_ActivityTips = {
    Text = [[
<Title:Event Overview>
1. During the event, Keepers can collect event currency "Soothing Incense," "Calming Incense," and "Dreamy Incense" through the limited-time gameplay "Week of Theophany" and "Achievement Rewards." "Soothing Incense," "Calming Incense," and "Dreamy Incense" can be used to purchase items in the "Holy Bedchamber," including the event-exclusive SR Wheel of Destiny "Blue-Ringed Toxin," Luminous Core, Pure Core, and more. 
2. Completing event achievements during the event will also grant the event-exclusive avatar "By the Silver Key: Murphy: Fauxborn"!

<Title:Event Duration>
1. From November 24th, 9:00 AM to December 15th, 9:00 AM (GMT+8), all event gameplay is available. 
2. From December 15th, 9:00 AM to December 22nd, 9:00 AM (GMT+8), only "Holy Bedchamber" and Achievement Rewards are available. 

<Title:Week of Theophany>
1. "Week of Theophany" includes 7 stages, with 1 stage automatically opening each day. 
2. Each challenge will consume 120 points of Menophin, and successful challenges will earn event currency. 
3. After clearing a stage, the "Reenact" feature for that stage will be unlocked. Note: Using the "Reenact" feature will not earn Affinity. 
4. You can use Alumnis assistance to help you clear stages more easily. 

<Title:Profane Carnival>
 After the event starts, you will automatically receive 60 "Soothing Incense" every hour, up to a maximum storage of 25 hours. 

<Title:Holy Bedchamber>
1. The "Holy Bedchamber" has three shops with the following opening times:
"Dream of Delight": Opens at 9:00 AM on November 24th.
"Dream of Godbirth": Opens at 9:00 AM on November 25th.
"Nightmare of Despair": Opens at 9:00 AM on November 26th. 
2. Each offering will consume 750 "Soothing Incense"/"Calming Incense"/"Dreamy Incense," randomly granting five item rewards from the bedchamber. 
3. Each bedchamber's item rewards are divided into "Special Items" and "Common Items." When resetting, you can reset the remaining quantity of special item rewards to the limit. The specific rules are: 
(1) For the first 2 resets: When there are no remaining "Special Items," Keepers can choose to reset, which will reset the remaining quantities of both "Special Items" and "Common Items" to the limit. They can also choose to continue offering, but when there are no remaining "Common Items," a reset is required to continue offering. 
(2) From the 3rd reset onwards: A reset can only be performed when there are no remaining "Common Items," which will reset the remaining quantities of "Common Items" to the limit. "Special Items" will no longer reset. 

<Title:Event Bonuses>
1. Keepers possessing specific Awakeners or Wheels of Destiny (not required to be deployed) can gain additional drop bonuses for "Soothing Incense," "Calming Incense," and "Dreamy Incense" in the "Week of Theophany" stage task rewards. The specific bonuses are as follows:
Awakener "Murphy: Fauxborn": Enlighten 0/1/2/3 and above, bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%.
SSR Wheel of Destiny "Uteri Somnia": Ascension 0/1/2/3 and above, bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%.
SR Wheel of Destiny "Blue-Ringed Toxin": Ascension 0/1/2/3 and above, bonus 20%/30%/40%/50%. 
2. Different Awakeners or Wheels of Destiny's "Event Bonuses" are calculated cumulatively. 
3. Notably, the first completion challenge rewards for Madness Difficulty will not be affected by "Event Bonuses."]]
